The bound HOLDS everywhere and is VACUOUS everywhere (slack 1e3-1e8).
Diagnosis, exactly: the pot sum_n z_n is dominated by the GAP times, where
z_n = 2^{R_n} > 2^c and grows, while on the corridor z_n <= 2^c.  Split it:
       m_0  c   occupied part           gap part  gap share
    285175  1       53.309737          96115.130   0.999446
    285175  2       87.279624          96081.160   0.999092
        27  1       10.037597              6.069   0.376809
       703  1        6.078821            436.700   0.986271
     10087  1       13.805562           7444.093   0.998149
     35655  1       11.928665          21791.993   0.999453

So amortizing the episode toll against the global carry pot can only bound
GAP time from above, i.e. it yields LOWER bounds on O_c, never upper ones.
Explicitly, with G = H - O_c the gap-time count and z_n > 2^c on gaps:
     2^c G  <  pot  ==>  O_c > H - 2^{-c} * pot    (a lower bound).
   m_0=   285175 c=1: 2^c G =       80.0 < pot =      96168.4  => O_c >     -47946.2  (actual O_c = 98)
   m_0=   285175 c=2: 2^c G =      112.0 < pot =      96168.4  => O_c >     -23904.1  (actual O_c = 110)
   m_0=       27 c=1: 2^c G =        2.0 < pot =         16.1  => O_c >         32.9  (actual O_c = 40)
   m_0=      703 c=1: 2^c G =       22.0 < pot =        442.8  => O_c >       -159.4  (actual O_c = 51)

